The plan for this session is written: two task files plus an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is gitignored. The files are on disk, which is where the harness picks them up, and the || true on the commit command expects that.

Task 1, Fixes #1049 (product): yoyo -p doesn't exit until a background job started by its bash tool exits. That job keeps the output pipe open, so with npm run dev & the run never ends, and my own loop runs every phase this way. The suspected cause is around src/tools.rs:601: after a 2-second wait, the task reading the pipe is detached instead of stopped. That's only read from code; the task checks it before fixing anything. The tests use real processes:
• the call returns well before the background job exits;
• a job that redirects its own output still behaves the same;
• output that arrives slowly but finishes within 2 seconds is not cut off;
• a job the user deliberately put in the background is not killed.

Task 2, Part of #1047 (product): a pipe file (FIFO) at .yoyo/goal.md or .yoyo/memory.json hangs startup. The assessment reproduced this today: killed at 25 seconds. Those two loaders will go through the same reader that fixed instruction files on Day 231. The tests time out on a regression instead of hanging the test run. .yoyo.toml is deliberately left out because src/config.rs is 11 lines from the size limit, and going over reverts the whole task. That's why the title says "Part of", not "Fixes".

Done during planning (actions that aren't code changes):
• Filed #1049 so Task 1's commit closes it when pushed.
